1
00:00:05,060 --> 00:00:07,730
Hello... motor insurance department...

2
00:00:07,730 --> 00:00:11,600
Oh hello... I'd like to ask about insurance for my car.

3
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:16,770
Yes, of course. I'll just take a few details. What's your name?

4
00:00:16,770 --> 00:00:18,240
Patrick Jones.

5
00:00:18,240 --> 00:00:20,000
And your address?

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,290
It's 27 Bank Road.

7
00:00:22,290 --> 00:00:27,570
27 Bank Road. Is that in Greendale?

8
00:00:27,570 --> 00:00:28,220
Yes.

9
00:00:28,220 --> 00:00:31,060
And what's your daytime phone number?

10
00:00:31,060 --> 00:00:35,950
My work number is 730453.

11
00:00:35,950 --> 00:00:39,430
And could I ask what your occupation is?

12
00:00:39,430 --> 00:00:40,360
Dentist.

13
00:00:40,360 --> 00:00:47,900
OK... now a few details about your car... What size is the engine?

14
00:00:47,900 --> 00:00:49,880
It's 1200 CCS.

15
00:00:49,880 --> 00:00:53,560
Thank you... and the make and model?

16
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:55,490
It's a Hewton Sable.

17
00:00:55,490 --> 00:00:59,170
Could you spell the model name please?

18
00:00:59,170 --> 00:01:03,000
Yes... S-A-B-L-E.

19
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:08,290
Ah yes, thanks. And when was it made?

20
00:01:08,290 --> 00:01:09,910
1997.

21
00:01:09,910 --> 00:01:16,350
Lovely... right... I presume you've had a previous insurer?

22
00:01:16,350 --> 00:01:17,000
Yes.

23
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:21,150
Right... we need to know the name of the company.

24
00:01:21,150 --> 00:01:24,560
Yes... it was Northern Star.

25
00:01:24,560 --> 00:01:31,200
Thank you, and have you made any insurance claims in the last five years?

26
00:01:31,200 --> 00:01:35,310
Yes... one in 1999.

27
00:01:35,310 --> 00:01:37,060
And what was the problem?

28
00:01:37,060 --> 00:01:39,250
It was stolen... but...

29
00:01:39,250 --> 00:01:43,760
That's fine, Mr Jones... that's all we need to know at the moment...

30
00:01:43,760 --> 00:01:48,000
And will there be any other named drivers?

31
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:49,150
Just the one...

32
00:01:49,150 --> 00:01:51,100
And his name?

33
00:01:51,100 --> 00:01:52,870
Simon Paynter.

34
00:01:52,870 --> 00:01:56,200
Could you spell the surname please?

35
00:01:56,200 --> 00:02:00,800
P-A-Y-N-T-E-R.

36
00:02:00,800 --> 00:02:07,330
OK thank you... And what relationship is he to you?

37
00:02:07,330 --> 00:02:09,000
He's my brother-in-law.

38
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:14,000
And what will you or Mr Paynter be using the car for?

39
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:17,770
Well... mainly for social use...

40
00:02:17,770 --> 00:02:24,040
Social use (murmuring). Will you be using it to travel to work?

41
00:02:24,040 --> 00:02:29,770
Yes... sometimes.

42
00:02:29,770 --> 00:02:31,500
... Anything else?

43
00:02:31,500 --> 00:02:33,150
No. That's it...

44
00:02:33,150 --> 00:02:38,000
And finally... when would you like to start the insurance?

45
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:40,600
I'll need it from the 31st of January.

46
00:02:40,600 --> 00:02:48,421
Right... Mr Jones... I'm getting a couple of quotes coming up on the computer now...

47
00:02:48,421 --> 00:02:55,200
and the best bet looks like being with a company called Red Flag.

48
00:02:55,200 --> 00:02:55,860
Yeah.

49
00:02:55,860 --> 00:03:01,600
And that comes out at $450 per year...

50
00:03:01,600 --> 00:03:07,910
Well... that seems OK... it's quite a bit lower than I've been paying up to now...

51
00:03:07,910 --> 00:03:11,860
Great... so would you like me to go ahead with that?

52
00:03:11,860 --> 00:03:13,150
Sure... why not?

53
00:03:13,150 --> 00:03:15,560
How would you like to pay?
